    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSX816/network-coordinator-tiny-uk-network": {
      "title": "Network Coordinator- Tiny UK Network",
      "description": "Network Coordinator- Tiny UK Network at Nottingham Trent University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Network Coordinator- Tiny UK Network Nottingham Trent University - School of Science and Technology Location: Nottingham Salary: £33,739 to £38,825\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 14th September 2026 Closes: 5th October 2026 Job Ref: 552475 Full time/ Fixed term contract for 12 months Important Information: This is an in-person post based in Nottingham. It involves collaboration with other EPSRC-funded networks and international partners. The role requires regular travel across the UK and abroad to support workshops, co-creation activities, tutorials, Hackathons and national level events. About TinyML UK TinyML UK is a new national network funded by UKRI through EPSRC. It connects researchers, industry, engineers, AI specialists and government organisations working on decentralised, energy-efficient machine learning for small and low-power devices. The Network supports collaboration, training, events and real-world impact across health, sustainability and security, while contributing to a UK roadmap for TinyML research and skills. The Network is led by Professor Eiman Kanjo at Nottingham Trent University, with co-leads Professor Geoff Merrett at the University of Southampton and Professor Pantelis Georgiou at Imperial College London. Role overview We are seeking a proactive and service-focused Network Coordinator to provide reliable operational, administrative and project support to the Network Lead and leadership team. The postholder will help deliver agreed priorities and activities, using initiative to complete assigned work, identify issues and propose improvements within the Network’s strategic direction. Key responsibilities Coordinate the Network’s day-to-day administration and operations. Support large and small events, workshops, training, competitions, meetings and outreach activities. The opportunity to lead activities. Maintain project plans, records, reports, budgets and stakeholder communications. Liaise with academic, industry, government and international partners. Support funding bids, partnerships, laboratories and related academic or institutional initiatives. Provide responsive support to the Network Lead, leadership team and wider consortium. Learn new skills and use AI and digital tools to improve project delivery. Undertake other reasonable duties consistent with the role’s purpose and grade as priorities develop. This is a full-time, 12-month fixed-term post, with the possibility of extension subject to continued funding, performance and operational requirements. Regular workplace attendance and occasional UK or international travel may be required. Further information is available at : https://tinyML.uk Interview date: Mid October 2026 (exact date TBC) Please click the 'Apply' button above to refer to the  job description and person specification for full details. About Us The School of Science and Technology at Nottingham Trent University (NTU) is an exciting multidisciplinary environment for learning, teaching and research, with some of the best facilities in the UK. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality teaching and diverse, real-world research. We specialise in biosciences, chemistry, computing and technology, as well as engineering, forensic science, mathematics, physics and sport science. This mix of traditional and modern subjects encourages and inspires future innovators. Our Department of Computer Science combines internationally-significant research with an outstanding record for teaching excellence. Our state-of-the-art facilities and career-focused approach to course design provide the right conditions for students to excel in their chosen fields. For any informal queries about the role or the team, please contact Prof. Eiman Kanjo Head of Smart Sensing Lab at eiman.kanjo@ntu.ac.uk Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunately, your alert was not created at this time. Please try ag